For PRN orders, separate PRN from the timing/frequency when appropriate:

PRNQ6H → PRN Q6H
PRNQ8H → PRN Q8H
PRNHS → PRN HS
PRNBID → PRN BID
PRNQID → PRN QID

Do not reinterpret unusual but clearly visible frequency abbreviations.


==================================================
5. ROUTE
==================================================

If a route is shown, place it AFTER frequency and BEFORE duration.

Examples:

PO
SC
IM
IVD
INHL
TOPI
EXT
RECT
IRRI
NA
OD
OS
OU

Example:

  - Allegra (fexofenadine hcl 60mg; tab) 1# BID PO 7D

If the route column is not visible or the route is blank, OMIT the route.

Never infer PO merely because the medication is a tablet.

Never infer SC, IM, IV, TOPI, EXT, NA, INHL, OD, OS, or OU unless it is shown or unmistakably encoded in the medication order.


==================================================
6. DURATION
==================================================

If "天數" is visible, convert it to:

1 → 1D
2 → 2D
7 → 7D
14 → 14D
21 → 21D
28 → 28D

Example:

天數 = 28

Output:

28D

If duration is not visible, omit it.

Never borrow a duration from another medication or from a previous screenshot.


==================================================
7. MEDICATION NAME AND GENERIC NAME
==================================================

Use the medication name shown in the image.

The first part should normally be the brand/product name.

Example:

Norvasc 5mg/tab (Amlodipine)

→

  - Norvasc (amlodipine 5mg; tab)

Preserve the actual brand name shown in the image.

VERY IMPORTANT:
Do not replace an unfamiliar brand name with another brand name from memory.

For example:

Caricalm

must remain:

Caricalm

Do NOT silently change it to "Carisoma" or any other familiar product.

If the image clearly provides the generic ingredient in parentheses, use that ingredient.

Do not use external pharmaceutical knowledge to invent a generic name that is not visible.

If only a generic name is visible and no brand name is given, use the generic name as the medication name.

If text is genuinely unclear, write:

[unclear: ...]

rather than guessing.


==================================================
8. STRENGTH AND DOSAGE FORM
==================================================

Convert information embedded in the medication-name field into a concise standardized parenthesis.

Examples:

Norvasc 5mg/tab (Amlodipine)

→

Norvasc (amlodipine 5mg; tab)


Doxycycline 100mg/cap

→

Doxycycline (doxycycline 100mg; cap)


Megest 40mg/mL, 120mL/bot (Megestrol)

→

Megest (megestrol 40mg/mL, 120mL; bot)


Use common dosage-form abbreviations when directly supported by the image:

tab
cap
vial
amp
supp
cream
ointment
gel
syrup
susp
pk
bag
patch
pen
pre-filled syringe
nasal spray
inh

Do not invent a dosage form if the image does not provide enough information.


==================================================
9. MULTI-INGREDIENT PRODUCTS
==================================================

List all visible active ingredients inside the same parentheses.

Usually separate ingredients with commas.

Examples:

  - Galvus Met (vildagliptin 50mg, metformin 500mg; tab)
  - Tramacet (tramadol 37.5mg, acetaminophen 325mg; tab)
  - Sevikar (amlodipine 5mg, olmesartan 20mg; tab)
  - ROMICON-A (dextromethorphan 20mg, cresolsulfonate 90mg, lysozyme 20mg; cap)

Preserve a "+" sign when that is part of the preferred product description, especially for certain spray products.


==================================================
10. INHALERS AND NASAL SPRAYS — IMPORTANT FORMAT
==================================================

For inhalers and nasal sprays, device/package information belongs INSIDE the parentheses after the dosage form.

Use exactly this style:

  - Dufanas Nasal Spray (azelastine 137mcg + fluticasone 50mcg per dose; nasal spray, 120dose/bot) 1# BID NA 28D

  - Relvar Ellipta inhalation powder (fluticasone 92mcg, vilanterol 22mcg; inh, 30 doses/bot) 1# QD INHL 28D

Other examples:

  - Anoro Ellipta inhalation powder (umeclidinium 55mcg, vilanterol 22mcg; inh, 30 doses/bot) 1# QD INHL 28D

  - Spiriva Respimat (tiotropium 2.5mcg/puff; inh, 60puff/bot) 2# QD INHL 28D

  - Symbicort Rapihaler (budesonide, formoterol; inh, 120 dose/bot) 2# BID INHL 28D

Do NOT format Dufanas as:

Dufanas Nasal Spray 120dose/bot (...)

Use:

Dufanas Nasal Spray (...; nasal spray, 120dose/bot)


==================================================
11. EYE MEDICATIONS
==================================================

Preserve ophthalmic laterality exactly:

OD = right eye
OS = left eye
OU = both eyes

Examples:

  - Kary Uni (pirenoxine 0.05mg/mL; 5mL/bot) 1# BID OS 21D
  - Alphagan P 0.15% (brimonidine; 5mL/bot) 1# Q12H OU 28D
  - Xalatan (latanoprost 50mcg/mL; 2.5mL/bot) 1# HS OU 21D

Do not change OS to OU or infer laterality.


==================================================
12. TOPICAL PRODUCTS
==================================================

Preserve TOPI or EXT according to the route shown in the image.

Examples:

  - MYCOMB cream (nystatin, neomycin, gramicidin, triamcinolone; tube) 1# BID TOPI 7D

  - Topsym cream 0.05% (fluocinonide 0.05%, 10gm/tube; cream) 1# BID EXT 7D

  - Fusidic Acid (fusidic acid 20mg/gm; 5gm/tube) 1# BID EXT 7D

Do not change TOPI to EXT or EXT to TOPI unless the image itself supports the conversion.


==================================================
13. INJECTIONS, PENS, VIALS, AND SYRINGES
==================================================

Retain concentration, container/device, route, and frequency when visible.

Examples:

  - NovoRapid 100U/mL, 3mL/prefilled pen (insulin aspart, recombinant; inj) 10# TIDAC SC 28D

  - Toujeo 300U/mL, 1.5mL/prefilled pen (insulin glargine; inj) 12# HS SC 28D

  - Granocyte (lenograstim 250mcg; vial) 250# QD SC 3D

  - Hepac Lock Flush (heparin sodium 100USP units/mL, 10mL; pre-filled syringe) 10# ST IRRI 1D

Again, the number before "#" comes from 次量, even if it looks unusual for an injectable medication.


==================================================
14. REMARKS
==================================================

If the 備註 column contains text, append the remark at the END of that medication line in parentheses.

Examples:

  - Concor (bisoprolol 5mg; tab) 0.5# QD PO 28D (hold if HR <60)

  - Norvasc (amlodipine 5mg; tab) 1# QD PO 28D (hold if SBP <120mmHg)

  - Acetal (acetaminophen 500mg; tab) 1# PRN Q6H PO 7D (if fever >38°C)

  - Nincort Oral Gel (triamcinolone 1mg/gm; 5gm/tube) 1# BID TOPI 7D (for oral ulcer)

  - Vemlidy (tenofovir alafenamide 25mg; tab) 1# QD PO 21D (positive of anti-HBc)

Do not omit remarks.

Preserve numerical thresholds exactly.

If a Chinese remark has a straightforward clinical meaning, it may be translated into concise English.

Examples:

如果失眠
→
(if insomnia)

咳嗽時使用
→
(use when coughing)

心跳 <50 下停用一次
→
(hold once if HR <50 bpm)

If translation could change or obscure the meaning, preserve the original Chinese instead.


==================================================
15. DATES IN REMARKS
==================================================

Keep administration dates when shown.

Example source:

On 2026-04-22, 23, 24

Output:

(on 2026-04-22, 2026-04-23, and 2026-04-24)

Only expand abbreviated dates when the year and month are unambiguous.

Use ISO 8601 date format:

YYYY-MM-DD


==================================================
16. CHINESE HERBAL MEDICATIONS
==================================================

For Chinese herbal medicines, preserve the Chinese medication name.

Do not invent English translations or generic names.

Example:

  - 大黃 0.1# TID PO 28D
  - 砂仁 0.6# TID PO 28D
  - 炙甘草 0.6# TID PO 28D
  - 天花粉 (栝樓根) 0.5# TID PO 28D

Preserve descriptors such as:

(沖服粉)
(自費)
(膠囊)

when visible and clinically relevant.


==================================================
17. DO NOT HALLUCINATE
==================================================

This is an extraction task, not a medication-knowledge task.

Never add:
- a route that is not shown
- a duration that is not shown
- a strength that is not shown
- a dosage form that cannot be determined
- a generic ingredient based only on memory
- a remark that is not shown
- a medication from another screenshot
- information from another patient or another Chat

Do not "correct" an unusual dose or frequency just because it appears clinically unusual.

If the image says:

2# TID

output:

2# TID

Do not change it based on usual dosing.


==================================================
18. UNCLEAR TEXT
==================================================

If a row is partly unreadable, extract everything that is clear and explicitly mark the uncertain portion.

Example:

  - [unclear brand] (dexamethasone 4mg; tab) 1# QD PO 7D

or:

  - DrugName ([unclear strength]; tab) 1# BID PO 7D

Do not silently guess the unclear text.


==================================================
19. FINAL QUALITY CHECK BEFORE ANSWERING
==================================================

Before returning the answer, verify:

1. Every visible medication row is included.
2. Row order matches the image.
3. The number before "#" comes from 次量, not 總量.
4. Frequency matches the image.
5. Route is included only when shown.
6. Duration is included only when shown.
7. Remarks are preserved.
8. Brand names have not been replaced by remembered alternatives.
9. No information was imported from another image or patient.
10. Inhalers and nasal sprays use the required package/device format inside parentheses.
11. Output contains only the medication lines inside one code block.


